  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The shrink rules",
      "items": [
        "Picked by tool name: a file keeps its outline and the lines about the task, a log its errors and last 50 lines, a search its first 50 lines",
        "Still over DISTILL_MAX_TOKENS? The gate model shortens the plain prose; never code blocks, tables, headings, paths or numbers with units",
        "Text under DISTILL_MIN_TOKENS is left alone; a condition_prompt call has no tool name, so only the model step applies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Saved results and the guard",
      "items": [
        "With SEMCACHE=on, very similar text counts as seen before",
        "Skills shrink only with DISTILL_SKILLS=on; a sentence the guard finds missing is kept verbatim from then on",
        "If a local model is slow or down, the text goes on as it was, with a note saying which step failed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Open decisions",
      "items": [
        "Low-risk answers found in your files are added as decided; the rest become questions for you, with a suggested answer",
        "Without a toolbox the gate offers condition_prompt, which runs the same steps on text you send it"
      ]
    }
  ]
